WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.669 --> 00:00:05.560
If you're curious about the long-awaited threequel
to Bad Boys, and some of the drama surrounding

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:06.520
it, look no further.

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:10.960
Here's everything you need to know before
you sit down to watch some massive explosions

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:12.540
and ridiculous action scenes.

00:00:13.940 --> 00:00:18.280
It just wouldn't be a Bad Boys film if it
weren't for the bad boys themselves, Will

00:00:18.280 --> 00:00:19.320
Smith and Martin Lawrence.

00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:24.140
Obviously, both Smith and Lawrence are returning
in their franchise roles as detectives Mike

00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:28.710
Lowrey and Marcus Burnett, and they'll still
use extreme measures to combat some of the

00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:30.100
worst crime in Miami.

00:00:30.270 --> 00:00:34.700
If you need a refresher, Will Smith's character,
Mike Lowrey, is the rich ladies man of the

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:38.920
team, while Lawrence's Marcus Burnett is more
the exasperated family man.

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:41.840
Together, they're the bad boys of the Miami
Police Department.

00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:46.900
There's one other crucial aspect to the Bad
Boys franchise, and that's the irritated,

00:00:46.909 --> 00:00:49.379
and grudgingly respectful, Captain Howard.

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:53.460
Luckily, Joe Pantoliano will also be returning
in Bad Boys for Life.

00:00:53.740 --> 00:00:57.700
We're guessing that time hasn't changed how
fed up he is with our favorite detectives,

00:00:57.940 --> 00:01:00.240
even if he always ends up having their backs
anyway.

00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:07.840
I got three cops critical, kids dying on the
street from souped-up X. I do not want these

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:09.680
animals taking over my city!"

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:14.540
We know a bit of the story going into Bad
Boys for Life, thanks to some official production

00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:16.680
notes and the trailers released so far.

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:21.200
The story focuses on AMMO, an elite squad
within the Miami Police Department.

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:26.120
Their current target is Armando Armas, a violent
young cartel leader.

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:30.600
Armas has his crosshairs focused on Detective
Lowrey, and he has a prior history with our

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:31.100
heroes.

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:35.760
With Armas on the hunt, Lowrey and Burnett
are pulled back into the fray, despite the

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:38.300
fact that Burnett seems to have his eye on
retirement.

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:42.580
They start working with AMMO's leader to stop
the threat that Armas poses.

00:01:42.860 --> 00:01:48.100
Naturally, AMMO's leader is also a former
flame of Detective Lowrey's, and he considers

00:01:48.109 --> 00:01:49.960
her the one that got away.

00:01:51.179 --> 00:01:55.509
Most of the actors showing up in Bad Boys
for Life are new to the franchise, but there's

00:01:55.509 --> 00:01:58.800
a pretty good mix of up-and-coming actors
and well-established ones.

00:01:59.340 --> 00:02:04.300
The big one joining the cast is Jacob Scipio,
who will portray Armando Armas, the film's

00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:04.800
villain.

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:10.119
His character is described as having a "vicious,
taunting nature" and he has a past connection

00:02:10.120 --> 00:02:10.760
with our detectives.

00:02:11.220 --> 00:02:16.080
Paola Nunez, a star of Mexican television
and film, is also joining Bad Boys for Life

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:20.080
as Mike's ex, a criminal psychologist and
the aforementioned head of AMMO.

00:02:20.580 --> 00:02:25.650
We also know a few actors who will play roles
as members of this elite squad: Vanessa Hudgens,

00:02:25.650 --> 00:02:29.120
Alexander Ludwig, and Charles Melton will
all be part of the team.

00:02:29.209 --> 00:02:33.900
It's a Bad Boys film, so it probably isn't
much of a stretch to guess that at least one

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:35.160
of them is a secret bad guy.

00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:40.300
Finally, one interesting wrinkle in the plot
description is that Armas targets our heroes

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:41.900
under the direction of his mother.

00:02:42.120 --> 00:02:46.540
We don't know for sure who plays this character,
but Kate del Castillo, who has been cast in

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:49.080
an undisclosed role, seems like a good bet.

00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:54.780
It seems like all the elements for a Bad Boys
film are here, but Bad Boys for Life is missing

00:02:54.780 --> 00:02:57.140
one significant piece: Michael Bay.

00:02:57.500 --> 00:03:02.180
Instead, the directing duo of Adil El Arbi
and Bilall Fallah are at the helm.

00:03:02.180 --> 00:03:07.440
They previously directed Black, Gangsta, and
have also signed to direct Beverly Hills Cop

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:07.940
4.

00:03:08.060 --> 00:03:11.960
They may not have been the first choices to
take on Bad Boys for Life, but they were the

00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:14.840
ones who managed to get the troubled production
to the finish line.

00:03:15.140 --> 00:03:19.580
Why did it take so long for a third Bad Boys
movie to explode onto the screen?

00:03:19.580 --> 00:03:22.260
Well, the project had to sail some troubled
waters.

00:03:22.540 --> 00:03:26.980
Will Smith has reportedly had a sequel in
mind since at least 2008, but multiple delays

00:03:26.989 --> 00:03:29.409
had many people thinking it may never happen
at all.

00:03:29.409 --> 00:03:33.880
The original director was going to be Joe
Carnahan, who's helmed big action movies like

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:35.660
Smokin' Aces and The A-Team.

00:03:35.860 --> 00:03:39.760
However, Carnahan apparently clashed with
Will Smith about the creative direction of

00:03:39.760 --> 00:03:43.220
Bad Boys for Life, and was subsequently let
go from the project.

00:03:43.640 --> 00:03:48.540
It's unclear exactly what caused the rift,
but Carnahan is still credited as co-writer

00:03:48.540 --> 00:03:49.580
on the film's screenplay.

00:03:51.140 --> 00:03:55.520
Considering all the talk in the trailer of
this being "the last ride" for our detective

00:03:55.520 --> 00:03:59.080
heroes, it seems likely that Bad Boys for
Life is the end of their story.

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:04.640
However, if they decide to ever truly reboot
the Bad Boys franchise, one Hollywood actor

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:07.280
has already thrown his name in the ring to
take up the reins.

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:12.860
Winston Duke, who played M'Baku in Black Panther
and starred in Jordan Peele's Us, told the

00:04:12.880 --> 00:04:16.640
The Deadline Podcast that he would love to
star if they ever rebooted Bad Boys.

00:04:16.780 --> 00:04:21.280
He also offered Black Panther co-star, Daniel
Kaluuya, as the person he would choose to

00:04:21.280 --> 00:04:24.100
partner up with if it ever did get off the
ground.

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:28.720
Considering the timing, it seems unlikely
that a Bad Boys reboot will happen any time

00:04:28.720 --> 00:04:33.260
soon, but the prospect of Duke and Kaluuya
teaming up is a great idea nonetheless.

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:38.280
With all the years that have passed since
Bad Boys II, you're probably eager to see

00:04:38.280 --> 00:04:39.730
some things blow up already.

00:04:39.730 --> 00:04:43.660
The trailers released so far have pretty much
everything you could want.

00:04:43.660 --> 00:04:45.580
Lowery exasperated at Burnett's antics?

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:46.120
Check.

00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:46.860
"I got this.

00:04:46.860 --> 00:04:49.880
I'm gonna penetrate this man's soul with my
heart."

00:04:49.880 --> 00:04:50.380
"What?"

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:52.600
Captain Howard swearing a whole bunch?

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:53.380
Check.

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:56.380
A bunch of people singing "Bad Boys" by Inner
Circle?

00:04:56.520 --> 00:04:57.200
Oh, yes.

00:04:57.520 --> 00:04:59.560
And, of course, the explosions.

00:04:59.720 --> 00:05:01.480
So many explosions.

00:05:01.820 --> 00:05:06.620
You'll be able to see them all when the film
blasts into theaters on January 17th, 2020.

